This gives you instructions to build and install the PHP plugin for dataman:

### Building it ###

You do not need to rebuild PHP. The normal supported method is to compile a shared extension with phpize, install the resulting .so, and enable it in PHP configuration.
PHP’s official phpize instructions (https://www.php.net/manual/en/install.pecl.phpize.php) describe this workflow.

after installing the dataman source:

cd /path/to/dataman/clientlib/php

phpize
./configure --with-dataman=/usr/local
make -j
make test

Using /usr/local is correct if the C client library has been built and installed in the default location:
/usr/local/include/dataman/dataman.h
/usr/local/lib/libdataman.so

At present you should skip

make test

because the file and index the tests use have not yet been included

For a temporary development test:

php -n \
  -d extension=/path/to/dataman/clientlib/php/modules/dataman.so \
  -r 'var_dump(extension_loaded("dataman"));'

And:

php -n \
  -d extension=/path/to/dataman/clientlib/php/modules/dataman.so \
  --ri dataman

### Installing it into PHP ###

Install the shared object:

cd /path/to/dataman/clientlib/php

php-config --extension-dir should report something similar to:

/usr/lib/php/20240924

so make install should place dataman.so in your extension-dir directory.

as root:

make install

Then create the PHP module configuration (assuming your php version is 8.4):

echo 'extension=dataman' |
    sudo tee /etc/php/8.4/mods-available/dataman.ini

Enable it for the installed PHP 8.4 SAPIs (as root):

phpenmod -v 8.4 dataman

Verify CLI loading:

php -m | grep -i dataman
php --ri dataman

For web use, restart whichever PHP service is active (on systemd systems):

sudo systemctl restart php8.4-fpm

or, for Apache’s PHP module:

sudo systemctl restart apache2

PHP extensions are enabled separately for each SAPI. It is possible for CLI PHP to
load the extension while PHP-FPM or Apache does not, so php --ini only verifies the CLI
configuration. PHP’s documentation also notes that the web service must be restarted
after enabling a newly installed shared extension. PHP extension installation overview
(https://www.php.net/manual/en/install.pecl.intro.php)

One ongoing requirement: PHP extensions are tied to PHP’s module ABI. When the system
upgrades to a PHP release with a different extension API directory, rebuild and
reinstall dataman.so using that release’s phpize and php-config.
